From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 16:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] winewayland: Start toplevels at the scale of their output.

A new toplevel started at scale 1.0 and waited for the compositor's
preferred scale. Mutter did not send it again for the toplevel Wine
recreates when a game switches from fullscreen to borderless, so on an
output scaled to 133% the logical 1920x1200 configure became the window
size, the 2560x1600 window was "too large for Wayland state", and only its
top-left 1920x1200 was shown until the output scale changed (Warframe,
#975). Start a toplevel at the scale of the output its window is on, as
layer surfaces already do; the compositor's preferred scale still
replaces it.

https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/975
---
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland_surface.c
@@ -1641,6 +1641,28 @@
 }
 
 /**********************************************************************
+ *          toplevel_initial_scale
+ *
+ * Returns the scale of the output the window is on, for a toplevel that has
+ * not received a preferred scale from the compositor yet.
+ */
+static double toplevel_initial_scale(const RECT *rect)
+{
+    struct wayland_output *output;
+    double scale = 1.0;
+
+    if (!process_wayland.wp_fractional_scale_manager_v1) return scale;
+    if (!(output = wayland_output_for_rect(rect))) return scale;
+
+    if (output->current.current_mode && output->current.logical_w > 0)
+        scale = round(120.0 * output->current.current_mode->width /
+                      output->current.logical_w) / 120.0;
+    wayland_output_release(output);
+
+    return scale;
+}
+
+/**********************************************************************
  *          wayland_surface_make_toplevel
  *
  * Gives the toplevel role to a plain wayland surface.
@@ -1713,7 +1735,13 @@
 
     wayland_surface_assign_icon(surface);
 
-    wayland_surface_init_fractional_scale(surface, 1.0);
+    /* The compositor is not required to send its preferred scale again for
+     * a toplevel recreated on the same output: mutter did not when a game
+     * switched from fullscreen to borderless. At scale 1.0 on a fractionally
+     * scaled output, the logical configure size becomes the window size and
+     * only the top-left part of the window is shown. Start at the output's
+     * scale; the compositor's preferred scale still replaces it. */
+    wayland_surface_init_fractional_scale(surface, toplevel_initial_scale(&surface->window.rect));
 
     wayland_surface_sync_alpha(surface);
 
--
